{title: Morning Paper}
{artist: Freevia Demo}
{composer: Freevia Demo}
{lyricist: Freevia Demo}
{key: C}
{tempo: 108}
{time: 4/4}
{comment: Original demonstration lyrics and illustrative chord chart created for Freevia; no recording or synced timing supplied.}

{start_of_intro}
[C] [F] [Am] [G]
{end_of_intro}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C]Sunlight slips be[F]neath the door,
[Am]Draws a golden [G]line across the floor.
[C]Coffee sings its [F]little tune,
[Am]We have time before the [G]afternoon.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_pre_chorus}
[Dm]Leave the clock upon the [F]wall,
[G]Let the quiet morning call.
{end_of_pre_chorus}

{start_of_chorus}
[C]Turn another [G]page with me,
[Am]There is more than [F]we can see.
[C]Every ordinary [G]day can start
[F]Something bright in a [G]tired old [C]heart.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C]Bicycles beside the [F]square,
[Am]Someone stops to [G]fix a folding chair.
[C]Tiny kindness, [F]nothing grand,
[Am]Passes like a letter [G]hand to hand.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C]Turn another [G]page with me,
[Am]There is more than [F]we can see.
[C]Every ordinary [G]day can start
[F]Something bright in a [G]tired old [C]heart.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge}
[Dm]Not a headline, [Am]not a race,
[F]Just a smile on a [G]familiar face.
[Dm]All the little [Am]things we do
[F]Make a morning [G]feel like new.
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus}
[C]Turn another [G]page with me,
[Am]There is more than [F]we can see.
[C]Every ordinary [G]day can start
[F]Something bright in a [G]tired old [C]heart.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_outro}
[F]Fold the paper, [G]come and [C]see.
[F]Save a little [G]light for [C]me.
{end_of_outro}
